g (0.123958ms)\n✔ version gaps and invalid first events reject without changing state (0.296667ms)\n✔ a CANCELLED trade is terminal and rejects later new versions (0.116208ms)\n✔ malformed events reject with TypeError; invalid field values rejected (0.194958ms)\n✔ returned states and snapshots do not expose mutable internal state (0.113625ms)\nℹ tests 8\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 8\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 63.911292\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787544607106},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 8 tests pass. Now completing INCIDENT.md:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"write:10","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/INCIDENT.md","content":"# Event projector incident\n\nStatus: resolved\n\n## Impact\n\n- A single temporary persistence rejection permanently poisoned the projector:\n  the shared promise chain stayed rejected, so every subsequent `project()` call\n  for every trade rejected forever.\n- State was committed to memory *before* persistence, so a rejected write left\n  a phantom committed state that was never stored.\n- One global promise chain serialized all trades: a slow store write for one\n  trade blocked unrelated trades.\n- No version or event validation: version gaps, stale events, events for\n  cancelled trades, and malformed payloads were silently accepted.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`project()` chained every event onto one module-level `pending` promise and did\n`states.set(...)` before `await applyToStore(...)`. A rejection therefore (a)\nleft the shared chain rejected with no recovery branch, and (b) left uncommitted\nin-memory state behind. There was also no `reduceEvent` guard for version\nsequence, terminal status, or payload validity.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Per-trade queues (`tails` map keyed by `tradeId`), each recovering from a\n  prior rejection via `.catch(() => {})` before chaining, so one trade's\n  failure never blocks or poisons other trades — or its own later events.\n- In-memory state now commits only after `applyToStore` succeeds; a rejection\n  leaves the previous state untouched.\n- `reduceEvent` now enforces: first event must be `CREATED` at version 1;\n  accepted versions are exactly `current + 1`; duplicate/stale versions return\n  the current snapshot without persisting; gaps and invalid first events\n  reject; `CANCELLED` is terminal; `CREATED` requires positive finite\n  `notional` and non-empty `owner`; `AMENDED` must leave a valid complete\n  state; unknown/malformed events throw `TypeError`.\n- Events are deep-cloned on intake and all returned states/snapshots are\n  `structuredClone` copies, so no mutable internal state escapes.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\n`student-tests.mjs` adds five tests:\n\n1. Different trades progress concurrently while one trade's store write is blocked.\n2. Duplicate/stale versions return the current snapshot without extra persistence calls.\n3. Version gaps and invalid first events reject without changing state.\n4. A `CANCELLED` trade rejects later new versions (terminal).\n5. Malformed events and invalid field values reject with `TypeError`.\n6. Returned states, snapshots, and input events do not expose mutable internal state.\n\n(The committed `event-projector.test.mjs` covers per-trade serialization and\nthe rejection-not-poisoning path.)\n\n## Remaining risk\n\n- The per-trade `tails` map retains an entry per tradeId forever; a projector\n  handling unbounded distinct trade IDs would grow memory. Entries could be\n  pruned once a tail settles, at the cost of extra bookkeeping.\n- `applyToStore` is invoked serially per trade but the store itself is\n  responsible for its own atomicity across trades; the projector cannot detect\n  a store that partially applies a write before rejecting.\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"moonshotai/kimi-k3","usage":{"input":704,"output":739,"cacheRead":7680,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3,"totalTokens":9123,"cost":{"input":0.002112,"output":0.011085000000000001,"cacheRead":0.002304,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.015501000000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787544607106,"responseId":"gen-1787544607-bhLtDK1hv94Nt5RXgttL","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"write:10","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 3008 bytes to benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/INCIDENT.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787544618481},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Verify final test run once more (already did). Done. Summarize.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Done. Final verification already shown above: **8/8 tests pass**.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Root cause** — `event-projector.mjs` chained all events onto one global `pending` promise and called `states.set()` *before* `await applyToStore()`. A single store rejection left the shared chain rejected forever (poisoning all trades) and left phantom committed state; additionally there was no version, terminal-status, or payload validation.\n\n**Repair** (`benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs`):\n- Per-trade promise chains (`tails` map) with `.catch(() => {})` recovery, so trades proceed concurrently and one failure never poisons later work.\n- In-memory state commits only after `applyToStore` succeeds.\n- `reduceEvent` enforces: first event = `CREATED` v1; accepted version = current+1; duplicate/stale → return snapshot without persisting; gaps/invalid-first reject; `CANCELLED` is terminal; `CREATED` requires positive finite `notional` + non-empty `owner`; `AMENDED` must leave valid state; malformed events → `TypeError`.\n- All inputs and returned states/snapshots are `structuredClone` copies.\n\n**Tests added** — 5 regression tests in `student-tests.mjs`: cross-trade concurrency, duplicate/stale no-persist, gap/invalid-first rejection, terminal `CANCELLED`, malformed/invalid-field `TypeError`s, and mutation-isolation of inputs/returns/snapshots.\n\n**Visible test result**:\n```\n✔ 8 tests, pass 8, fail 0  (2 committed + 6 student tests)\n```\n\n**Remaining risk** — the per-trade `tails` map grows unboundedly with distinct trade IDs (no pruning of settled tails), and the projector cannot guard against a store that partially applies a write before rejecting."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"moonshotai/kimi-k3","usage":{"input":979,"output":417,"cacheRead":8192,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":18,"totalTokens":9588,"cost":{"input":0.002937,"output":0.006255,"cacheRead":0.0024576,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0116496}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787544618482,"responseId":"gen-1787544618-y9iRib4oBGez6rn6LBX9","rawStopReason":"stop"}],"willRetry":false}
